{"kind":"report","text":"Adopt the G2p prerequisite, with the refinements below. This is a pre-Source decision for the new bounded query path only. It is not approval of frozen G2r bfd3b6e7, a public query, legacy admission changes, deployment or full G2. Checked current Main ff846e495973c49b4c0b60c0a2cc96d3719f227a, including core.ts pinned/validate/platform, sessions.ts authentication/prepare/allows, authority.ts recordedMembership/repositorySessionBirth/resolve, worker.ts sessionWiring, SQLite readers and the exact platform catalog callbacks.\n\n1. The diagnosis is supported. core.ts pinned() loads and JSON-parses stored(0) before definition validation and fetches retained definition bytes before validate(). ScopeObject's legacy genesis callback does the same. SqliteStore.scope/item/page/retained materialize unrestricted JSON rows. sessions prepare authenticates before inspecting membership, but the authenticated local callbacks can still invoke those readers; worker sessionWiring resolves the actual birth directory through full summary(). A bounded query must have its own bounded preparation dependencies, with no call or fallback to those legacy bodies. Retain existing public routes and their behavior. Share small pure validation/policy logic rather than copy the Scope implementation or add a second membership policy.\n\n2. Approve initial support limits: 4 KiB direct current-scope metadata, 1 MiB exact genesis through the reviewed G2r reader contract, 256 KiB retained declared-definition bytes, and for the supported platform membership/birth read-only facade 16 storage-read calls, 16 total metadata candidates and 256 KiB cumulative item/fold body bytes. Count repeated reads and lookahead, all merge candidates, anchors and post-await revalidation; reserve their costs before issuing the work. Metadata/key/time/hash fields, argument shapes and counts need their own finite admission too. These are initial supported-operation limits, not an assertion that every legal room, declaration or native history fits. Missing, corrupt, unsupported and exhausted support are private unknown/unavailable and cannot confer authority or reveal size/state/head/readiness to an unproved signed caller. Separate missing from malformed/oversized current metadata internally, as in G2s. No total heap, global concurrency, physical I/O or full object-lifecycle bound follows just from these body limits.\n\n3. For pinned content, admit truthful direct-column UTF-8 length before transfer or parse, then verify actual admitted bytes, strict form/canonical identity, full own ScopeRef/incarnation and genesis seq/hash against current ScopeState.genesis. Read and validate status/time/head fields actually needed, under the scope-row allowance. A declared definition must match definitionDigest under DOMAINS.definition, not a raw text or entry digest; use the same validator, profiles, derivable/counted capability support and runtime bounds as normal whole-definition support. For a platform pin, use the exact closed runtime VERSIONS entry and the existing trusted platform validation/runnable/whole-capability checks, never NEWEST or a prefix/name alias. An untrusted retained/input declaration never acquires the platform validation option. Read-only support must not invoke old pinned(), generic genesis/store reads, source/resolver, judgments or outside work. A validated immutable definition cache may key full own genesis identity, exact declaration digest or platform version, plus validator/capability/runtime-bound policy version. Bound its count and bytes. Cache successful content/support only; missing content may arrive later. Do not cache clock, current head/status, session claims or member/key standing as immutable definition data.\n\n4. The facade must reproduce the existing exact-version callback semantics on one synchronous coherent local head; expose only its admitted methods, with unsupported access stopping the operation. Actual read-only does not mean merely a Pick over the old Store. In particular current incarnations(scope) executes DISTINCT json_extract over folded records with no scope lookup index; LIMIT on its output or a bounded returned array does not prove bounded underlying work. Supply a genuinely bounded native seek/proof for zero/one/multiple observed incarnations, or report this supported operation unavailable. referenceOf needs only distinguish zero, one and more than one, but must not label a truncated same-incarnation prefix complete. Avoid a new whole-table index build or scan in cold construction/read preparation; any necessary legacy index population needs its own bounded maintenance/completeness ownership. Item state pages must use metadata-first indexed candidates including lookahead, preserve first-ID ordering and more, and never silently truncate what an authority callback interprets as complete. Require actual SQLite seek/candidate/body-transfer evidence for these paths, including large unrelated populations.\n\n5. Preserve the existing child-birth cohort and asymmetric checks. repositorySessionBirth derives the peer only from the caller's applied genesis, seed.kind/creator/source/create message and its locally held directory reference, with an exact SIBLINGS_OF child pin supported by platform(). Session claims cannot select or replace the peer. After any await recheck current incarnation/genesis, catalog/policy and the current recorded membership binding; final query state/head and its response must be coherent. If a concurrent head change requires fresh preparation, allow only a bounded retry or fail unavailable. Existing rules fallback additionally requires the directory's confirmed rules target to equal this rules ScopeRef. Existing destination fallback intentionally does not make that same target-equality check; do not silently impose or remove it in this support change. Reuse the current version callbacks for held membership/rules references rather than infer membership from a room chain, scope name, creator alone or a newer cohort.\n\n6. Adopt a dedicated deployment-internal read-only directory session-reference RPC. Receiver first uses the existing bounded session-token MAC/form/deployment checks, then bounded local scope/clock/pinned/catalog/membership preparation and the same summary-read compatibility as the existing directory summary. It must require the token's summary claim for this fallback and match its membership to the directory's own full confirmed reference; a new query claim is no substitute. Preserve local clock/expiry ordering and indistinguishable private failures. Receiver checks its full expected directory identity/incarnation, active status and exact supported pin, and exactly one open repository record using bounded indexed metadata with a second-candidate witness; reading the first record alone loses the old resolve() cardinality test. Authenticate and establish the existing repository read authority before releasing any proof. Return only a strictly versioned small reference witness: its own full directory identity, exact catalog pin and the full confirmed membership reference, plus the rules target where needed to preserve the existing check. Necessary identity/cohort binding fields are part of the reference witness, not permission to return summaries, item bodies/counts, state inventories or origin/source material. Clamp request, reply and receiver work limits in native code; caller checks the full envelope/identity/catalog/reference and its own current birth/membership again. The RPC is not an externally routable arbitrary-reference reader, does not call #first/driver/old summary/pinned()/origin/backfill, and must not recursively discover a membership peer. Unsupported bounded peer capability fails unavailable, without old summary fallback. Trace activation and callback dependencies too; omitting #first alone does not establish bounded read preparation.\n\n7. Budget the entire operation across local preparation, one exact peer and revalidation, with an absolute completion deadline and bounded pending/singleflight ownership. Do not restart an allowance at each callback or await. A timeout races completion and prevents late cache/authority success; it is not a claim of physical RPC cancellation. Reuse immutable birth-reference caching only with the full own incarnation/genesis, exact birth directory/cohort and current recorded ID/incarnation guards, as the current session reader does; it creates no grant/observation and does not stand in for fresh token MAC/deployment/clock/read checks. Preserve current session revocation semantics: issued claims remain valid until their expiry; do not turn this optimization into fresh roster/role authority or early revocation. Required ordinary-session claims remain summary for live items, items for final items, both for a mixed request. An unresolved birth fallback also retains the existing additional summary-claim requirement. Recent-local signer OR exact-genesis-root bootstrap eligibility remains separate and unchanged; neither grants final rows.\n\n8. Split into two independently reviewable Source children before public-query integration. G2p-a owns bounded scope/genesis/retained-definition and facade storage support, immutable cache/policy keying, candidate/incarnation seek semantics and actual native SQLite tests, with no public caller switch. G2p-b owns bounded session preparation and the narrow directory reference RPC, exact cohort parity, receiver/caller authentication/revalidation and deadline/pending ownership, using the reviewed storage child. G2r remains a separately reviewed dependency. Use native current platform versions in parity witnesses, manually restricted live/final/mixed sessions and unresolved birth cases; include wrong repository/incarnation/pin, expired/clock-behind, duplicate open repository, ambiguous observed incarnation, oversized/malformed pre-transfer rows, changing head and late/unavailable peer cases. Controls must fail by asserting the unwanted read/authority/wake behavior and restore exact source; synthetic storage rows do not prove native judgments. Preserve the single original gate and focused-correction qualifications for each submitted Source; no mutation sweep or repeated whole suite is requested.","body":{"formal_approval":"false","promise":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:bc50b590dc59536e9c25dce7a9e064c9cdef00a8","scope":"G2p pre-Source bounded definition and session-reference support decision"}}